      "tip": "Suppresses Office's First Run Opt-in Wizard and 'First things first' recommended-settings prompt, sets diagnostic data to the lowest level (Neither), and opts out of feedback requests, in-product surveys, and the Watson-based proofing tools data collection. Applies per-user (HKCU) - only affects Office once it's installed. Opt-in and reversible. Every value verified against admx.help's real Office 2016/365 ADMX definitions (office\\16.0\\common\\clienttelemetry, common\\feedback, common\\ptwatson, common\\general) - note OptInDisable lives under the policy-backed Common\\General key while ShownFirstRunOptin is a separate, non-policy Common\\General key with the same name.",
